            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A cup remover instrument assembly for removing an acetabular cup in a revision hip procedure comprising: a positioning member supporting a cutting assembly having a cutting blade and a detachable drive member for selectively rotating the cutting assembly to cut around a cup to detach the cup from a patient's natural acetabulum. In embodiments, the positioning member is sized and configured to operate in a main incision, while the drive member is sized and configured to operate in a portal incision. In embodiments, the cutting blade is detachable for use in selecting blades for cup sizes. In embodiments, the cutting blade is selectively extendable from the cutting assembly. In other embodiments, the cutting blade is hemispherical and is rotated by a power driver.</p>
            </abstract>
